
# The terminal host (terminal-target-0002): the dom contract for a program drawn in a terminal's cells. The tree is the
# memory host's, so every node operation the render runtime calls (create, set, append, remove, replace, listen) is
# the one the differential test already holds on four backends (test/compile/render-native.ts), and ./paint reads that
# tree into the cell grid. A terminal has no document, so the page tasks are the memory host's no-ops as well.
# The contract is note/term/view/12-render-seam.md.

bear ../memory/dom
bear ./paint
bear ./focus
bear ./input
bear ./keys

# ./app, the loop that owns a real terminal, is loaded by the program that wants it rather than borne here: its natives
# are node's and Rust's only, and the host itself compiles on every backend
